{"availability":"available","full":"Hearthlight/hearthlight.github.io","name":"hearthlight.github.io","description":"A cozy pixel-art adventure in the browser (a demo): a story in ten chapters, eight heroes, Party Mode for 1–8 players with phones as controllers. Everything procedural.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":30,"forks":11,"created":"2026-09-28T17:32:45Z","updated":"2026-10-13T07:49:43Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hearthlight.github.io/","topics":["game","javascript","party-game","pixel-art","procedural-generation","threejs"],"demo":"https://hearthlight.github.io/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T13:32:28.931Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T13:32:28.931Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T13:32:28.931Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:40:17.919Z","stars":28,"forks":11},{"at":"2026-10-15T23:48:00.485Z","stars":29,"forks":11},{"at":"2026-10-18T13:32:28.931Z","stars":30,"forks":11}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A cozy little life in Marigold Cove — and a big adventure beyond it.","This is a demo. Hearthlight is a hobby project, playable from start to end, but it hasn't been tested all the way through by real players yet: the ten chapters, the eight heroes and Party Mode were played by test bots, not by crowds. Expect rough edges, a balance to tune and the odd bug — and please tell us about them in the issues.","Hearthlight is a calm, funny, story-driven pixel-art game. Make your character, pick your hero, settle into a seaside village — then follow the lights out of the valley into two continents, ten chapters of story, dungeons and bosses, alone or with up to eight friends on one screen, the phones as controllers. Every sprite, texture, model and sound is made in code: there isn't a single image or audio file in the game."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Hearthlight/hearthlight.github.io/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1